KG42.register("source_edge_archive-ca5c0dde79ba71d5d8e461ed",{"id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E002","paper":"07-nash_bargaining","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","rule_ref":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R003","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","target":"COMP-10be07664c6496b7","source_occurrence_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","target_occurrence_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","source_unit_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","target_unit_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Energy-quantity reporting during the decentralized P1 iterations among interconnected microgrids. | Payment reporting by participating interconnected microgrids during the decentralized solution of P2. | Virtual clearing house coordination at the beginning of each daily operation of the interconnected-microgrid market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"30ea8f4cdb2390a3ffabf23aec8895db1ec903cf900b9a0ceb37800fb3877d54","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Offered information and submission conditions in this mechanism: P1 first minimizes interconnected microgrids total operating cost and fixes bilateral energy; P2 maximizes the product of net gains of the active trading set through payment bargaining.","target_definition":"Virtual clearing house receives P1 energy schedules and P2 payments and updates auxiliary/dual signals. Energy and payment stages remain separate objects.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Microgrids submit the offered quantities in their selling schedules to the virtual clearing house. Scope: Energy-quantity reporting during the decentralized P1 iterations among interconnected microgrids. Condition: For reported schedule entries with e_{i,j}^t \u003c 0, representing sales by microgrid i to microgrid j.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E37"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e27","location":{"location_id":"src-7e85444402-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Energy Trading Among Microgrids","anchor_text":"We consider that each microgrid i ∈M bargains with all the other interconnected microgrids to determ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We consider that each microgrid i ∈ M bargains with all the other interconnected microgrids to determine the amount of energy trading e_i = {e_{i,j}^t, ∀t ∈ T, ∀j ∈ M\\i} and the associated payment π_i = {π_{i,j}, ∀j ∈ M\\i}. Here e_{i,j}^t denotes the amount of energy that microgrid i exchanges with microgrid j in time slot t, and π_{i,j} denotes the associated payment for energy trading between microgrid i and microgrid j. If microgrid i purchases energy from microgrid j in time slot t, then e_{i,j}^t > 0; otherwise, microgrid i sells energy to microgrid j and e_{i,j}^t \u003c 0. Similarly, if microgrid i makes payment to microgrid j, then π_{i,j} > 0; otherwise microgrid i receives payment from microgrid j and π_{i,j} \u003c 0. 4Note that the payments π_i are determined through bargaining between microgrids, and are not necessary linear in terms of the energy exchange e_i."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E37","location":{"location_id":"src-7e85444402-p08-c2r4__v141-a-M01-activation","page":8,"printed_page":"2654","section":"V.C Algorithm Design and Implementation","anchor_text":"To implement the solution method for solving the energy trading and payment problems P1 and P2, we d","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We introduce the concept of virtual clearing house for solving the higher level problem. The virtual clearing house is a communication and computing module, which provides clearing service of energy trading and payment for all the microgrids. At the beginning of each daily operation, the virtual clearing house updates the auxiliary and dual variables according to (21), (22) and (25), (26), and broadcasts to all participating microgrids when solving P1 and P2, respectively. All the participating microgrids concurrently solve P1-MGi and P2-MGi and report their energy trading schedules and payments to the virtual clearing house."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Energy-quantity reporting during the decentralized P1 iterations among interconnected microgrids. | Payment reporting by participating interconnected microgrids during the decentralized solution of P2. | Virtual clearing house coordination at the beginning of each daily operation of the interconnected-microgrid market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"paper_scope_note":"Distinguish the interfaces of P1 dispatch, P2 payment, the actual transaction set, and the clearing institution; the same clearing institution does not mean that the variables of P1 and P2 can be merged."}});
